title "Figures"

The parabola appears in @fig-a.

figure "images/parabola.png" width 70% #fig-a
  alt "The parabola y equals x squared, opening upwards through the origin, with axes."
  The graph of $y = x^2$ on $[-1.2, 1.2]$.

figure "images/filtered.png" width 40%
  alt "The same parabola, re-encoded with PNG row filters."
  Row filters.

figure "images/parabola.jpg" width 40%
  alt "The parabola as a JPEG."
  A JPEG, passed through untouched to the PDF, with a caption long enough to need more than one line of text to be set.

figure "images/palette.png" width 30%
  alt "Palette PNG."
  Palette.

figure "images/gray16.png" width 30%
  alt "16-bit grayscale."
  Sixteen bits.

figure "images/grayalpha.png" width 30%
  alt "Gray with alpha."
  Gray and alpha.

figure "images/bits.png" width 10%
  alt "A one-bit pattern."
  One bit.

figure "images/gray.jpg" width 30%
  alt "Gray JPEG."
  Gray JPEG.
